    {
      "title": "IFC 300 Supplementary instructions: Description of Modbus interface",
      "version": "4000410703 R03, 07/2010",
      "url": "https://cdn.krohne.com/pick2/tagged_docs/AD_IFC300_Modbus_en_100709_4000410703_R03.pdf",
      "note": "chapter 6, Modbus protocol",
      "accessed": "2026-11-15",
      "sha256": "9a71a5e2b6abe8abd8809f90a84748b8ea981ef9ef17108332a54804fdcf55df"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Modbus RTU on RS485. Defaults: address 1, 19200 bit/s, even parity, 1 stop bit, big-endian data (C5.8.1-C5.8.6).",
    "The listed addresses are protocol addresses and are sent as listed (input register 30006 is address 30006). Each block is also reachable without its leading digit (input registers 0-37, holding registers 0-3036) and the calibration result at 9000 instead of 20000.",
    "Floats are IEEE 754, big endian by default; holding register 50004 switches the device to little endian.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's document; not tested on a device."
  ],
  "protocol": "rtu",
  "unit_id": 1,
  "baudrate": 19200,
  "parity": "E",
  "stopbits": 1,
  "byte_order": "big",
